<title>DUBAI: Oman cuts July crude selling price to $17.46.</title>
<headline>Oman cuts July crude selling price to $17.46.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-08-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has cut the official selling price of its crude oil lifted in July to $17.46 a barrel from $17.75 in the previous month, an Omani oil official said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Non-OPEC Oman sets its selling price in line with spot market developments.</p>
<p>- Dubai newsroom, +971 4 6071222</p>
</text>
